@anon.3c5d4856225436a016f648d8ca8332b3.3171 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [2785 x i8] }> <{ [2785 x i8] c"# `transparent_unions`\0A\0AThe tracking issue for this feature is [#60405]\0A\0A[#60405]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/60405\0A\0A----\0A\0AThe `transparent_unions` feature allows you mark `union`s as\0A`#[repr(transparent)]`. A `union` may be `#[repr(transparent)]` in exactly the\0Asame conditions in which a `struct` may be `#[repr(transparent)]` (generally,\0Athis means the `union` must have exactly one non-zero-sized field). Some\0Aconcrete illustrations follow.\0A\0A```rust\0A#![feature(transparent_unions)]\0A\0A// This union has the same representation as `f32`.\0A#[repr(transparent)]\0Aunion SingleFieldUnion {\0A    field: f32,\0A}\0A\0A// This union has the same representation as `usize`.\0A#[repr(transparent)]\0Aunion MultiFieldUnion {\0A    field: usize,\0A    nothing: (),\0A}\0A```\0A\0AFor consistency with transparent `struct`s, `union`s must have exactly one\0Anon-zero-sized field. If all fields are zero-sized, the `union` must not be\0A`#[repr(transparent)]`:\0A\0A```rust\0A#![feature(transparent_unions)]\0A\0A// This (non-transparent) union is already valid in stable Rust:\0Apub union GoodUnion {\0A    pub nothing: (),\0A}\0A\0A// Error: transparent union needs exactly one non-zero-sized field, but has 0\0A// #[repr(transparent)]\0A// pub union BadUnion {\0A//     pub nothing: (),\0A// }\0A```\0A\0AThe one exception is if the `union` is generic over `T` and has a field of type\0A`T`, it may be `#[repr(transparent)]` even if `T` is a zero-sized type:\0A\0A```rust\0A#![feature(transparent_unions)]\0A\0A// This union has the same representation as `T`.\0A#[repr(transparent)]\0Apub union GenericUnion<T: Copy> { // Unions with non-`Copy` fields are unstable.\0A    pub field: T,\0A    pub nothing: (),\0A}\0A\0A// This is okay even though `()` is a zero-sized type.\0Apub const THIS_IS_OKAY: GenericUnion<()> = GenericUnion { field: () };\0A```\0A\0ALike transparent `struct`s, a transparent `union` of type `U` has the same\0Alayout, size, and ABI as its single non-ZST field. If it is generic over a type\0A`T`, and all its fields are ZSTs except for exactly one field of type `T`, then\0Ait has the same layout and ABI as `T` (even if `T` is a ZST when monomorphized).\0A\0ALike transparent `struct`s, transparent `union`s are FFI-safe if and only if\0Atheir underlying representation type is also FFI-safe.\0A\0AA `union` may not be eligible for the same nonnull-style optimizations that a\0A`struct` or `enum` (with the same fields) are eligible for. Adding\0A`#[repr(transparent)]` to  `union` does not change this. To give a more concrete\0Aexample, it is unspecified whether `size_of::<T>()` is equal to\0A`size_of::<Option<T>>()`, where `T` is a `union` (regardless of whether or not\0Ait is transparent). The Rust compiler is free to perform this optimization if\0Apossible, but is not required to, and different compiler versions may differ in\0Atheir application of these optimizations.\0A" }>, align 1
